From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:08:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: Skip the startables a device lists

On Deckard's container SystemUI stays only for the window manager shell
(the IME's control target for per-app windows); its bars, keyguard and
most other parts never show. Let ro.deckard.skip_systemui_startables
name CoreStartables to leave out by simple class name ($ for nested
classes). They are not created and count as started, so startables
that depend on them still run. The list is the device's to measure
and keep.

Change-Id: I3bd399244045e550085a305da380fae7b2a913b4
---
 .../impl/SystemUIApplicationImpl.java         | 34 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/application/impl/SystemUIApplicationImpl.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/application/impl/SystemUIApplicationImpl.java
index 00887f7b4..5fa7df5f0 100644
